<!--
  Author: Kris Hollingsworth
  Class: Math122-Calculus 2
  Date: 5/24/26
  File: E01-C06-01-AnswerValidation.oml
  Description:
    Some progress checks on an ODE word problem.
  Raw Link: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DoctorHaitch/doenet-math-problems/main/M122-Calculus-2/E01-C06-01-AnswerValidation.oml
-->

<cascade>
<section>
  <title></title>
Define your notation:
<p>
  Dependent Variable: <mathInput name="depVar"/><br/>
  Independent Variable: <mathInput name="indVar"/><br/>
</p>


<p>
  Differential equation that models this problem:
  <answer name="ansDiffEq">
    <shortDescription>Enter differential equation.</shortDescription>
    <award>
      <m>\frac{d$depVar}{d$indVar} = \frac{30-$depVar}{125}</m>
    </award>
    <award>
      <m>$depVar' = \frac{30-$depVar}{125}</m>
    </award>
  </answer>
</p>
<setup>
  <boolean name="ansOneIsExpression">
    not(<matchesPattern pattern="＿=＿">$ansDiffEq</matchesPattern>)
    and
    <matchesPattern pattern="()">$ansDiffEq</matchesPattern>
  </boolean>
</setup>
<feedback condition="$ansOneIsExpression">
  It seems you've entered an expression.
  Looking back at the definition of a differential equation, it should be a <em>function</em>, which by definition is a relationship between indepedent and dependent variables.
</feedback>
</section>

<section>
  <title></title>
<p>
  General solution:
  <answer name="genSoln">
    <shortDescription>Enter general solution.</shortDescription>
    <award>
      <m>$depVar' = Ce^{\frac{-2$indVar}{25}}+3</m>
    </award>
    <award>
      <m>\frac{d$depVar}{d$indVar} = Ce^{\frac{-2$indVar}{25}}+3</m>
    </award>
  </answer>
</p>
<setup>
  <boolean name="genSolnIsExpression">
    not(<matchesPattern pattern="＿=＿">$genSoln</matchesPattern>)
    and
    <matchesPattern pattern="()">$genSoln</matchesPattern>
  </boolean>
</setup>
<feedback condition="$genSolnIsExpression">
  It seems you've entered an expression.
  Looking back at the definition of a differential equation, it should be a <em>function</em>, which by definition is a relationship between indepedent and dependent variables.
</feedback>
</section>

<section>
  <title></title>
<p>
  Particular solution:
  <answer name="partSoln">
    <shortDescription>Enter particular solution.</shortDescription>
    <award>
      <m>$depVar' = 57e^{\frac{-2$indVar}{25}}+3</m>
    </award>
    <award>
      <m>\frac{d$depVar}{d$indVar} = 57e^{\frac{-2$indVar}{25}}+3</m>
    </award>
  </answer>
</p>
<setup>
  <boolean name="partSolnIsExpression">
    not(<matchesPattern pattern="＿=＿">$partSoln</matchesPattern>)
    and
    <matchesPattern pattern="()">$partSoln</matchesPattern>
  </boolean>
</setup>
<feedback condition="$partSolnIsExpression">
  It seems you've entered an expression.
  Looking back at the definition of a differential equation, it should be a <em>function</em>, which by definition is a relationship between indepedent and dependent variables.
</feedback>
</section>

<section>
  <title></title>
<p>
  Answer the original question:
  <answer name="finalAns">
    <shortDescription>Answer to original question.</shortDescription>
    <award>
      <m>57e^{\frac{-2*90}{25}}+3</m>
    </award>
  </answer>
</p>
<feedback condition="$finalAns.creditAchieved">
  This is good for an automated system, but in your written work, the answer to a word problem should be a <em>sentence</em>! For example:<br/>
"The amount of salt in the tank after 90 minutes is <m>57 e^{-\frac{36}{5}}+3</m> kilograms."<br/>
  If you feel it necessary to round, indicate you have done so, but also give the precise answer, for example:<br/>
  "The amount of salt in the tank after 90 minutes is <m>57 e^{-\frac{36}{5}}+3</m> kilograms, or approximately 3.0426 kilograms."<br />
  You'll worry more about <em>significant digits</em> and how many digits to include in answers in your applied coursework.
</feedback>
</section>
</cascade>